     1,
     "\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<div dir=\"ltr\">\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Calibri,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\n<span style=\"font-family:Calibri,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">Hello! </span><br>\r\n</div>\r\n<div dir=\"ltr\">\r\n<div dir=\"ltr\">\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Calibri,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\n<span><a href=\"https://msuclanac-my.sharepoint.com/:u:/g/personal/lwgent_uclan_ac_uk/Ef5irkBWkHBCmajI0zvcCVsBPKyg_V8xcxWf3l1gSSEU9A\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" style=\"padding:0px 1px;border-radius:2px;background-color:rgb(243,242,241)\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://msuclanac-my.sharepoint.com/:u:/g/personal/lwgent_uclan_ac_uk/Ef5irkBWkHBCmajI0zvcCVsBPKyg_V8xcxWf3l1gSSEU9A&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793230783790000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3QY2a-yVsaf4ltt0NMQU0a\"><img alt=\"\" role=\"presentation\" style=\"width:16px;min-height:16px;vertical-align:middle;padding:1px 2px 2px 0px\" src=\"https://ci6.googleusercontent.com/proxy/lzPCtwTMx-al3oNxFj4o50JJrsHWwzVZakbAIw-cO95TznNfLsqaFUdB1UCgA8CwYC1lvAM_gG1iX1la9jJBCZSx_q4jEd_R5f57Rv_htrqDj9OPsSc9_j6eMqKOkg5ZhKse=s0-d-e1-ft#https://res-h3.public.cdn.office.net/assets/mail/file-icon/png/generic_16x16.png\">DefaultSettings.6_S6_L001_R1_001_val_1_bismark_bt2_pe.bismark.cov</a></span><br>\r\n </div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Calibri,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\nI&#39;m still quite new at looking at sequencing data, and I&#39;m currently just &#39;practicing&#39; lets say with a pilot sample from a project I&#39;m on with the methylKit package; so I&#39;m not sure if I&#39;ve read incorrectly but I may have caused a blunder for myself.</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Calibri,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\n<br>\r\n</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Calibri,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\n<br>\r\n</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Calibri,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\nI initially tried it out what I believe is the standard or a standard way of doing it with the .cov file from bismark_methylation_extractors outputs? Directly with readMeth:</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Calibri,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\n<br>\r\n</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Calibri,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\n<br>\r\n</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Calibri,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\nfile.list &lt;- list(  &quot;DefaultSettings.6_S6_L001_R1_001_val_1_bismark_bt2_pe.bismark.cov&quot;)</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Calibri,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\n<br>\r\n</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Calibri,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\nmyobj &lt;- methRead(file.list,</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Calibri,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\n<a href=\"http://sample.id\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://sample.id&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793230783790000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0ElaIq5XA4vKwCTu3LOLV8\">sample.id</a>=list(&quot;TestSample&quot;),</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Calibri,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\npipeline = &quot;bismarkCoverage&quot;,</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Calibri,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\nassembly=&quot;hg38&quot;, </div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Calibri,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\nmincov = 10,</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Calibri,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\ntreatment = 1,</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Calibri,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\ncontext = &quot;CpG&quot;)<br>\r\n</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Calibri,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\n<br>\r\n</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Calibri,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\n<br>\r\n</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Calibri,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\n^^So lets put this aside for now.^^</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Calibri,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\n<br>\r\n</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Calibri,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\n<br>\r\n</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Calibri,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\nI secondly instead just tried out the package with my BAM file with the aim of obtaining methylation rates for each of the positions with the processBismarkAln() function as I found a thread online that suggested it, like so:</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Calibri,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\n&#39;my.methRaw = processBismarkAln(location = &quot;/Users/lukeg/OneDrive - UCLan/miSeq/BAM/DefaultSettings.6_S6_L001_R1_001_val_1_bismark_bt2_pe.sorted.bam.bam&quot;,</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Calibri,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\n<a href=\"http://sample.id\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://sample.id&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793230783790000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0ElaIq5XA4vKwCTu3LOLV8\">sample.id</a> = &quot;test1&quot;, </div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Calibri,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\nassembly = &quot;hg38&quot;, </div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Calibri,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\nread.context = &quot;CpG&quot;,</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Calibri,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\nsave.folder = getwd())&#39;</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Calibri,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\n<br>\r\n</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Calibri,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\nThis created &#39;test1_CpG.txt&#39; which then I used methRead like so:</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Calibri,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\nfile.list=list(&quot;/Users/lukeg/OneDrive - UCLan/miSeq/BAM/m.gz&quot;)</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Calibri,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\n<br>\r\n</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Calibri,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\nmyobj2=methylKit::methRead(file.list[[1]],</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Calibri,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\n<a href=\"http://sample.id\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://sample.id&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793230783790000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0ElaIq5XA4vKwCTu3LOLV8\">sample.id</a>=&quot;test1&quot;, </div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Calibri,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\nassembly=&quot;hg38&quot;,</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Calibri,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\ntreatment=c(1), </div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Calibri,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\ncontext=&quot;CpG&quot;,</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Calibri,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\nmincov = 10)<br>\r\n</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Calibri,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\n<br>\r\n</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Calibri,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\nSo I have two &#39;myobj&#39; that were created differently, one via the .cov file and the other from the BAM after processBismarkAln. Seems both are the correct objects for the downstream steps, except they both have a different number of ranges, and the ranges of\r\n the same chromosome positions have different values when I create granges objects out of them with the worked out meth percentage values (I couldn&#39;t do it the standard way as the unite function to create the actual meth object instead of methraw is for if\r\n there are multiple samples in the BAM file). </div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Calibri,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\n<br>\r\n</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Calibri,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\nThis is an example of how I did it with the my.obj objects, I did the exact same thing with both:</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Calibri,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\n<br>\r\n</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Calibri,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\nmyobj.filt &lt;- filterByCoverage(myobj,</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Calibri,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\nlo.count=10, </div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Calibri,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\nlo.perc=NULL,</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Calibri,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\nhi.count=NULL, </div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Calibri,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\nhi.perc=99.9)</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Calibri,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\n<br>\r\n</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Calibri,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\nmyobj.filt.norm &lt;- normalizeCoverage(myobj.filt, method = &quot;median&quot;)getCoverageStats(myobj.filt.norm[[1]],</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Calibri,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\nplot=TRUE,both.strands=FALSE) </div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Calibri,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\n<br>\r\n</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Calibri,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\n<a href=\"http://my.gr\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://my.gr&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793230783790000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3DLm5Zju860wqbUKHj8Rgm\">my.gr</a> &lt;- as(myobj.filt.norm[[1]],&quot;GRanges&quot;)</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Calibri,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\n<a href=\"http://my.gr\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://my.gr&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793230783790000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3DLm5Zju860wqbUKHj8Rgm\">my.gr</a></div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Calibri,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\nmy.gr_df &lt;- as.data.frame(<a href=\"http://my.gr\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://my.gr&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793230783790000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3DLm5Zju860wqbUKHj8Rgm\">my.gr</a>)</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Calibri,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\nmy.gr_df$MethPerc &lt;- (my.gr_df$numCs/(my.gr_df$numCs + my.gr_df$numTs))</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Calibri,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\nmy.gr_methperc &lt;- FusionExpressionPlot::grAddColumn(<a href=\"http://my.gr\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://my.gr&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793230783790000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3DLm5Zju860wqbUKHj8Rgm\">my.gr</a>, &quot;MethPerc&quot;, my.gr_df$MethPerc)</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Calibri,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\n<br>\r\n</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Calibri,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\nlibrary(annotatr)# Get premade CpG annotationsbuiltin_annotations()</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Calibri,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\n<br>\r\n</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Calibri,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\nhg38_cpgs_annotations &lt;- build_annotations(genome = &#39;hg38&#39;, annotations = &quot;hg38_cpgs&quot;)</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Calibri,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\n<br>\r\n</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Calibri,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\nmy.gr_annotated &lt;- annotate_regions(  regions = my.gr_methperc,  annotations = hg38_cpgs_annotations,  ignore.strand = TRUE)</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Calibri,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\n<br>\r\n</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Calibri,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\nmy.gr_annotated</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Calibri,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\n<br>\r\n</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Calibri,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\nmy.gr_annotated_df &lt;- data.frame(my.gr_annotated)<br>\r\n</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Calibri,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\n<br>\r\n</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Calibri,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\n<br>\r\n</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Calibri,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\nApologies if this is nonsensical, both scripts I used are attached. The main issue is, the differences between the granges objects at the same range and understanding why one created more strands than the other. For example, in my.obj, chr1 125178955  differs\r\n in its numCs and numTs than in my.obj2. </div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Calibri,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\n<br>\r\n</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Calibri,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\nI&#39;m happy to answer any questions.</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Calibri,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\n<br>\r\n</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Calibri,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\nBest,</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Calibri,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\n<br>\r\n</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Calibri,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\nLuke Gent,</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Calibri,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\n<br>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Calibri,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\n<br>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0);background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">\r\n<div style=\"font-size:12pt;margin:0px;text-align:start;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">\r\n<span style=\"font-size:15px;margin:0px;color:rgb(36,36,36);background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\"><i><b><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif;margin:0px\">PhD R</span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif;margin:0px\">​</span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif;margin:0px\">esearcher\r\n in Forensic Science, </span></b></i></span>\r\n<div style=\"font-size:15px;margin:0px;color:rgb(36,36,36);background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">\r\n<span style=\"font-family:Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif;margin:0px\"><i><b>Department of Natural Sciences</b></i></span></div>\r\n<div style=\"font-size:15px;margin:0px;color:rgb(36,36,36);background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">\r\n<span style=\"font-family:Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif;margin:0px\"><i><b>Member of @Forens-OMICS Team, University of Central Lancashire.</b></i></span></div>\r\n</div>\r\n<span style=\"font-size:12pt;margin:0px;text-align:start;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\"><span style=\"font-size:15px;margin:0px;color:rgb(36,36,36);background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\"><img style=\"margin:0px;max-width:100%\" src=\"https://groups.google.com/group/methylkit_discussion/attach/390816a4afc0/Outlook-b5ncwkya.png?part=0.0.1&amp;view=1\"><img width=\"309\" height=\"100\" style=\"margin:0px;width:309px;min-height:100px\" src=\"https://groups.google.com/group/methylkit_discussion/attach/390816a4afc0/Outlook-vhylupwo.png?part=0.0.2&amp;view=1\"></span></span><br>\r\n</span></div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n"
    ]
   ]
